<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for May 3.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for May 3.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the transport and pipeline arm of BG plc has announced the following forecasts and data for UK gas consumption in the period May 1 to 3.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>May 1 (actual) 158 mcm, 37 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 2 (forecast) 152 mcm, 35 perecnt of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 3 (forecast) 141 mcm, 33 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>May 1 (actual) 15.9 Celsius, SNT 11.3 Celsius</p>
<p>May 2 (forecast) 15.4 Celsius, SNT 11.5 Celsius</p>
<p>May 3 (forecast) 16.3 Celsius, SNT 11.6 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Friday, with none expected for Saturday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
